+# FAA action and no-action records in released DOT OIG investigation files
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review UTC · B129 / PD02–PD05, supporting PD01. Two redacted DOT OIG reports in release **FI-2013-0123** show where an FAA action decision or recommendation response can be recorded. In one case, a supplemental report gives the date FAA advised OIG of administrative action, reports a separate no-action reason and separately records OIG closure. In another, a follow-up report identifies the earlier report and FAA response as an attachment and lists which recommendations FAA accepted and declined. These cases provide specific record types to look for in **CC-2006-085 / 042R0122001**. [Release letter, physical p. 2](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=2)
+
+| Released record | What was observed |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Northwest Mountain Region**, OIG case **I08A00035000903**, physical p. 24 lines 3–9, 19–20 and 36–43 | The face is dated **JAN 6 2010**, with status **Supplemental** and distribution **JRI-9 (1)**. The narrative cites the separate originating investigation **02IH452S001**. It reports that FAA advised OIG on **August 6, 2009** of administrative actions. The listed contents are redacted. The FAA notice and underlying decisions were not acquired. [Report face](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=24) |
+| **Same supplemental report**, physical p. 25 lines 1–12 | It reports a distinct FAA no-action decision because the items accepted were below the applicable annual amount, and describes a separate prosecution referral and later FAA administrative referral with intervening content redacted. The document then records OIG closure. The reason is what the report attributes to FAA. The threshold calculation and any later outcome on the referral remain unverified. The ten visible numbers across pp. 24–25 are list positions. Their redacted contents prevent identifying ten distinct employees or ten disciplinary measures. [Outcome and closing language](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=25) |
+| **San Juan**, physical pp. 175–177 | The August 25, 2011 final report identifies Attachment **4** as an OIG report dated **August 6, 2009** with the FAA response. It says FAA concurred with recommendations **1 and 2** and declined **3**, citing existing protocols, and that OIG provided the report to OSC in August 2009. The visible San Juan report ends before a new report starts on physical p. 181. Attachment 4 is identified by the inventory. Its actual contents, signed response and transmission remain unacquired. [Face and inventory](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=175) · [Disposition account, p. 177 lines 24–34](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=177) |
+
+## Preserve these distinctions
+
+- The same date **August 6, 2009** appears in both records. It is an FAA notification date in the Northwest Mountain narrative and the date of an earlier OIG report in the San Juan attachment inventory. The packet supplies no link between those documents.
+- San Juan's rendered cover reads **I11A002SINV**. The sorted text layer returns **`Il 1A002SINV`**. The title uses **Foreign Facility Deviations** and the allegation heading uses **Foreign Flight Deviations**. Preserve both identifier representations and both terms as source locators. [Physical pp. 175–176](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=175)
+- The release letter describes a narrowed request for the first ten pages from the primary report or memorandum of **51 investigations**, with some later resolution pages included and intervening pages omitted. The case files and their attachments have wider scope than the selected release. An attachment reference, an attributed FAA response and a case-closure statement answer separate questions. [Physical p. 2 lines 24–34](https://www.governmentattic.org/15docs/51DOT-OIGclosingDocs1stPages_2007-2012.pdf#page=2)
+
+## Next case-specific records
+
+- [ ] **PD02.** Seek the signed FAA decision or reasons for no action, the dated FAA notice to OIG and any supplemental report summarizing it. Verify who made the decision and which recommendation it addressed before treating a notice or case status as a completed action.
+- [ ] **PD03–PD05.** Seek a closing memorandum or supplemental report, correspondence and attachment inventory, and recommendation-specific status history for **042R0122001 / CC-2006-085**. Compare the records to dated outcomes in the investigative database and determine whether the applicable version, office and case type used these forms. This release shows examples of the form of the evidence. It leaves their applicability and the 2006 disposition open. [Earlier database lead](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/d0872692b6a0ea5c5b482abb9a658d0d045d8299/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-dot-investigations-notice-and-closing-2026-11-10/README.md)
+- [ ] **PD01.** Seek the actual corrected May 2003 answer, attachments and dated delivery acknowledgment. A follow-up report could identify them by date or attachment number. Track recommendations **1–2** separately from **3–4**. [Original recommendations, pp. 12–13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12)
+
+The newly preserved public release has **263 physical pages**, **39,279,094 bytes**, SHA-256 **8b88d20f136f93d7b0bb6c1e4ba04524307f08e4d02f41dff5fe79fbbb515340**. Selected page images and 15 text anchors were checked. An exact-text screen of all 263 pages gave zero matches for the 2006 report and case IDs and found the shared date on physical pp. 24 and 176. This screen has OCR, redaction and release-selection limits. The review found no 2006 decision or signed correction. [Source pins and checks](SOURCE-PINS.json)
